# Base Components Guide

The `base` directory contains shared components and utilities used across all applications.

## Integration

To use base components in an app:

1. Add the following to `nuxt.config.ts`:
```ts
import path from "path"
vite: {
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@base': path.resolve(__dirname, '../../base/app'),
    },
  },
}
```

2. Add the following to `tsconfig.json`:
```ts
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@base/*": [
        "../../base/app/*"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Base Structure

- **[base/app/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/base/app)**: Contains the shared components and utilities
- **[base/layers/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/base/layers)**: Contains additional feature layers
- **[base/plugins/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/base/plugins)**: Contains shared plugins

## Usage Example

Import base components using the `@base` alias:

```ts
import BaseComponent from '@base/components/BaseComponent.vue'
```
